; A misplaced tag in an imported module is reported in that module's
; own source. Here `TagStray` carries a `restrict(...)` tag above a
; `data` declaration and an `unhandled(trap)` tag above a function
; (AX3077 both), and both lines must point into `TagStray.ax`. The
; stray-tag pass runs before the body walk stamps each declaration's
; unit, so it stamps the unit itself.
;
; The entry file's own misplaced tag, on `Mode`, stays here.
(import TagStray)

;@axiom:restrict(no-io)
(data Mode
  (Fast)
  (Slow))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (halve 4))
